C) Solvency II SCR over one year

Create 13_scr_one_year.py:

def compute_one_year_scr(
    model: str,
    S_paths: np.ndarray,        # includes t=0..1y (and enough beyond to value BEL_1y)
    t_grid: np.ndarray,
    r_curve, q_curve,
    rila_params: dict,
    hedging_result: dict,       # from run_dynamic_hedge
) -> dict:
    """
    Compute Δ Own Funds over 1 year:
      OF_t = Assets_t - BEL_t
      ΔOF = OF_1y - OF_0
    Return: VaR_99.5, CTE_99.5 of (−ΔOF), plus summary stats.
    """


BEL_0: PV of RILA at t=0 (replication + model pricing).

BEL_1: Re-value at t=1 (given S(1), remaining T−1, rolled r/q curves) under same model.

Assets: Hedge cash + marked-to-market hedge positions at t=1 (include transaction costs).

Metrics: VaR 99.5% (0.5th percentile) and CTE 99.5% of −ΔOF; also report mean and stdev.

